#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:1
msgid "The document classification file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:3
msgid ""
"`metadata/document_classify.yaml` lets a formats repository recognise a "
"document's format from the document itself — from a line of its cover, a "
"typeface on its title page — rather than from the URL it was downloaded "
"from. `freeports-dev init-format-repo` creates it with no rules; a file "
"that is absent, empty or only comments classifies nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:8
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The grammar follows the format names ({doc}`names`): a name is a path "
"down a tree, and the file is written as that tree. This page is the "
"grammar. When the author needs logic the grammar cannot express, the "
"Python module of {doc}`document-classify-python` runs first and hands "
"over to this file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:12
msgid "The idea in one example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:25
msgid ""
"Read it top to bottom. On page 1: if a line begins `FONDI AMUNDI `, the "
"document is `AMUNDI-IT24` and the search ends. Otherwise, if a line "
"begins `KAIROS INTERNATIONAL SICAV`, it is `KAIROS-EN23`. Otherwise, if a"
" line begins `Mediolanum` or `MEDIOLANUM`, it is *some* `MEDIOLANUM` "
"format — not yet which — and the search goes on inside that block, where "
"the typeface of the title tells `.A` from `.B`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:31
msgid "Three ideas carry the whole grammar:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:33
msgid ""
"**Pages, then steps, both in the order written.** The first step that "
"settles a complete name ends the search."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:35
msgid ""
"**A step may settle only part of a name.** That partial result is kept, "
"and later steps can only refine it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:37
msgid ""
"**Nesting is context.** A step inside `MEDIOLANUM` is looked at only once"
" the document is known to be a `MEDIOLANUM` one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:40
msgid "Pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:42
msgid ""
"The top level lists the pages to look at, each with its steps. A page is "
"an integer: `1` is the first page, `-1` the last, `-2` the one before it;"
" there is no page `0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:45
msgid ""
"Pages are tried **in the order written**, not in numerical order, and the"
" search stops at the first page that settles a complete name. That order "
"is a statement about cost. Turning a page into lines is the expensive "
"part of classifying, so a file that puts page 1 first, and puts a later "
"page only where page 1 is not enough, usually reads a single page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:50
msgid ""
"A page the document does not have — page 5 of a four-page document — "
"gives nothing for that entry, and the search goes on. It is not an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:52
msgid ""
"The same page may appear more than once. It is read once per document, "
"and \"the same\" means the same physical page: on a ten-page document `1`"
" and `-10` are read once between them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:54
msgid ""
"Pages `1` and `-1` are the only ones every document has. That matters to "
"the load-time checks ([below](#what-is-refused-when-the-file-is-loaded))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:57
msgid "Steps and their criteria"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:59
msgid ""
"Under a page comes a sequence of **steps**. A step is a key — a format "
"name, complete or partial — and a body: the **criteria** a page must meet"
" for the step to match, and possibly **child steps**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:62
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A criterion is a line selection, written exactly as in the "
"semistructured level's YAML** — the mapping form of "
"{doc}`../../guides/formats/selections`, with the same keys (`text`, "
"`font`, `font_size`, `area`, `window`, `font_of`, `any_of`, `all_of`, "
"`without`). A criterion is met when it selects at least one line of the "
"page. Everything that page says holds here, in particular that text "
"anchors are verbatim strings with `^` and `$`, not regular expressions, "
"and that sizes are best written as ranges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:69
msgid "What document classification adds to selections is only this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:71
msgid ""
"A step's criteria are an **AND**: every one must select a line. The order"
" among them does not matter. Two criteria of one step are written as a "
"list, or as one mapping using `all_of`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:73
msgid ""
"An **OR** is written with `any_of` inside one criterion, or by repeating "
"the step further down — in which case the order of the two copies matters"
" like the order of any two steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:75
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A criterion that states nothing — `{}`, `{any_of: []}`, a `without` on "
"its own — is an error. It would select every line, and \"the page has "
"some text\" is not a fact about a format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:78
msgid "What a step does when it matches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "The step's name is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "When its criteria match"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "**complete** (`KAIROS-EN23`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "the document is that format, and the search ends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "**partial** (`MEDIOLANUM`, `FINECO-EN23@*`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid ""
"the partial name is kept as the **result so far**, and the search goes on"
" — into the step's children, then to the steps after it, then to the next"
" pages — looking for a more complete match"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:85
msgid ""
"The result so far is carried from one page to the next. The cover can say"
" the entity, and the table of contents the variant:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:97
msgid ""
"If the search ends on a partial name — nothing more complete was found — "
"that partial name is the outcome, and the formats of the repository it "
"still allows are the candidates to try."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:100
msgid "Which steps are looked at"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:102
msgid ""
"Once a partial result is held, a step is looked at only if its name "
"**refines** it: once the document is known to be `MEDIOLANUM`, a step for"
" `AMUNDI` is skipped, and so is a second `MEDIOLANUM` step, which would "
"add nothing. The result can only grow more precise; it is never replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:106
msgid ""
"That has a consequence worth writing down before writing the file: **a "
"partial match is sticky.** If a document of another group mentions "
"`Mediolanum` on its cover — as a distributor, say — then from that moment"
" no step of any other entity is looked at, on any page. Two habits "
"contain it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:110
msgid ""
"write the criteria of a partial step with the care of a complete one — "
"anchored, specific — because in effect they decide the entity;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:112
msgid ""
"put the partial steps of a page **after** the complete ones, so that a "
"document a complete step recognises outright never reaches them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:115
msgid "Nesting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:117
msgid ""
"A step's body may hold child steps after (or among) its criteria. A "
"child's key is not a whole name but a **suffix** that continues its "
"parent's name from the first segment the parent leaves open:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
