msgid "language, or language and year, optionally with place and variant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "`MEDIOLANUM` → `EN`, `IT23`, `ES24.*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "the language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "the year, optionally with place and variant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "`MEDIOLANUM-EN` → `23`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "`@*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "the place, with or without its `@`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "`FINECO-EN23@*` → `LUX` or `\"@LUX\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "`.*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "the variant, with or without its `.`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "`MEDIOLANUM-IT24.*` → `A` or `.A`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "`@*.*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid ""
"place or variant **with** its separator, since a bare `LUX` could be "
"either"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "`X-EN23@*.*` → `\"@LUX\"`, `.A`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "the year"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "nothing: a complete name has no children"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md
msgid "`FINECO-EN23` cannot have children; write `FINECO-EN23@*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:129
msgid ""
"A child must name a strictly more precise set than its parent, and it may"
" itself end in `@*` or `.*` and have children of its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:132
msgid ""
"**A nested block is context, not a shortcut.** A child is looked at only "
"once its block has been entered — once the result so far is at least as "
"precise as the nearest enclosing step that has criteria of its own. Where"
" no enclosing step has criteria, the top-level key plays that role. So a "
"generic criterion such as `text: Relazione` under `MEDIOLANUM` can never "
"fire on an Amundi report, and a child with criteria is context for its "
"own children in turn. A key with no criteria, which only spells part of "
"the name, filters nothing: adding or removing one changes no outcome."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:139
msgid "A step whose criteria fail closes its whole block for that page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:141
msgid "The unconditional step: `~`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:143
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A step with an empty body — `~`, `[]` or `{}` — has no criteria and "
"always matches. It is the **otherwise** of a block:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:154
msgid ""
"A format decided this way was decided **by exclusion**, and the engine "
"says so when it reports the result. The price is that the criteria of the"
" enclosing step now decide the format on their own for every document on "
"which `EN24` does not match — choose them with that in mind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:158
msgid ""
"An unconditional step with a **complete** name at the top level decides "
"every document still unclassified when it is reached. Every later step "
"that could only fire on an unclassified document is then dead, and the "
"load-time check reports each of them ([below](#what-is-refused-when-the-"
"file-is-loaded))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:163
msgid "The catch-all: `*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:165
msgid ""
"A top-level step whose entity is `*` completes whatever entity has "
"already been found:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:173
msgid ""
"`*-EN23` reads \"*the entity already found, in English, 2023*\". With "
"`MEDIOLANUM` held it stands for `MEDIOLANUM-EN23`, and its criteria are "
"checked only if the repository has that format. If the repository has no "
"`EN23` for the entity found — or no entity has been found — the step "
"simply does not fire, and the result so far stands. That is not an error,"
" at load time or at run time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:178
msgid ""
"A catch-all must write at least the language, appears only at the top "
"level, and has no children. It is an error only when **no entity of the "
"repository** could complete it — `\"*-DE23\"` in a repository without a "
"single `…-DE23`, or the slip `\"*-EN32\"` — because then it cannot be "
"anything but a typo."
msgstr ""

