#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:207
msgid ""
"Whether a key is a criterion or a child is decided by the key: selection "
"keys are lower-case words from the fixed list above, names are not. The "
"one place the two could meet is a variant named like a selection key "
"(`text`, `area`) under `.*`; write it with its separator, `.text`, to "
"make it a child."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:211
msgid ""
"Repeating a step — the OR of two copies of one step — needs the list "
"form, since a mapping cannot hold the same key twice. \"The same key\" is"
" judged on the names the keys stand for: `21` and `\"21\"`, `LUX` and "
"`\"@LUX\"` under `@*`, `A` and `.A` under `.*` are duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:215
msgid "What the YAML reader does to keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:217
msgid "The file is read as YAML 1.2, and three of its rules meet the grammar:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:219
msgid ""
"**`*` and `@` cannot begin an unquoted key**: `*` starts an alias, `@` is"
" reserved. Write `\"*-EN23\":` and `\"@LUX\":`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:221
msgid ""
"**Numbers are read as numbers.** `23:` is an integer and is accepted as a"
" year (`5:` becomes `05`) or as a variant (`1:` becomes `.1`). But "
"`24.10:` is the number `24.1`, and `true:` or `null:` are not text: such "
"keys are refused with the advice to quote them, because the spelling is "
"already lost. `08:` with a leading zero stays text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:225
msgid ""
"**The order of a mapping is kept.** That is what lets a mapping stand in "
"for a list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:227
msgid "What is refused when the file is loaded"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:229
msgid ""
"The file is checked against `metadata/formats.csv` as soon as the "
"repository is loaded, before any document is opened. The guarantee is "
"that **no complete result of the file can be a name the repository does "
"not declare**, and that no step was written that no document could ever "
"reach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:233
msgid ""
"Every message names the file and the place: the page, the enclosing steps"
" by their full names, and the key —"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/formats/document-classify-yaml.md:240
msgid ""
"A file with several defects reports all of them, one per line, in file "
"order, so one correction round fixes them all."
msgstr ""

